---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildSEOMeta, getHubUrl, getFullUrl } from '../../lib/seoEngine';

const lang = 'en';
const title = 'Privacy Policy — Zeit-Rechner.com';
const description = 'Privacy policy for Zeit-Rechner.com: what data is processed, how Google Analytics is used only with your consent, and the rights you have under the GDPR.';
const canonical = '/en/privacy-policy/';

// Flip to true once Google AdSense is approved and the ad code is live.
const adsEnabled = false;

const seo = buildSEOMeta('hub', lang, {}, canonical, 'de', '/datenschutz/', false);
seo.title = title;
seo.description = description;

const lastUpdated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });
---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  canonical={seo.canonical}
  hreflang={seo.hreflang}
  lang={lang}
  theme="info"
>
  <section class="section landing-hero" style="padding-bottom: 2rem;">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="landing-hero__lead">Transparent information about what data is processed when you visit this site — and what you decide for yourself.</p>
      <div class="last-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="content-prose legal-content animate-in">

        <h3>1. Controller</h3>
        <p>
          The controller for data processing on this website is the operator named in the
          <a href="/en/imprint/">imprint</a>, where you will also find the contact details for any privacy enquiries.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Principle: your calculations stay on your device</h3>
        <p>
          Every calculation on this site — time spans, working hours, countdowns, public holidays and bridge days —
          runs <strong>entirely locally in your browser</strong>. The values you enter are never transmitted to our
          servers or to third parties, and they are not stored.
        </p>

        <h3>3. Hosting and server log files</h3>
        <p>
          This website is hosted by Vercel Inc., 340 S Lemon Ave #4133, Walnut, CA 91789, USA. When pages are requested,
          Vercel processes technically necessary server log files, in particular IP address, date and time of the
          request, the requested URL, referrer, browser type and operating system. This processing is required to
          deliver the site securely and reliably and is based on our legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Transfers
          to the USA are covered by the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
        </p>

        <h3>4. Cookies and local storage</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>No cookies are required</strong> to operate the calculators. We only use the following storage:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Necessary (no consent required):</strong> your cookie choice and a few calculator interface
            preferences are kept in your browser's local storage. This data never leaves your device.
            Legal basis: § 25(2) TTDSG, Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Statistics (consent only):</strong> Google Analytics sets cookies or comparable identifiers —
            exclusively if you have agreed (see section 5).
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>5. Consent and Google Consent Mode</h3>
        <p>
          On your first visit we ask for your consent via a notice at the bottom of the page. Until you agree, all
          non-essential services are <strong>disabled by default</strong> ("denied" under Google Consent Mode v2) and
          the analytics script is not loaded at all. If you choose <em>"Essential only"</em>, it stays that way.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can change or withdraw your decision at any time using the <strong>"Cookie settings"</strong> link in the
          footer of every page. Withdrawal takes effect for the future; the lawfulness of processing carried out before
          withdrawal is unaffected.
        </p>

        <h3>6. Google Analytics (consent only)</h3>
        <p>
          With your consent we use Google Analytics 4, a web analytics service provided by Google Ireland Limited,
          Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. It helps us understand which calculators and content are
          used so we can improve the site.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Data processed includes a truncated IP address, device and browser information, pages viewed, time on page and referrer.</li>
          <li><strong>IP anonymisation is enabled</strong>; your IP address is truncated before any further processing.</li>
          <li>Transfer to Google LLC in the USA is possible, based on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</li>
          <li>Legal basis: your consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR and § 25(1) TTDSG.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          For more information see
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
          You can also prevent collection using
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's opt-out browser add-on</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>7. Advertising</h3>
        {adsEnabled ? (
          <>
            <p>
              With your consent we display advertising through Google AdSense (Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House,
              Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland). Google and its partners may set cookies or comparable identifiers to
              serve ads, measure their performance and — where you have agreed — show personalised advertising.
            </p>
            <p>
              The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, § 25(1) TTDSG), which you can withdraw at any time via
              "Cookie settings". You can manage your Google ad preferences at
              <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">adssettings.google.com</a>.
            </p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <p>
            <strong>No advertising is currently served</strong> on this website and no advertising cookies are set.
            Should this change, we will update this section in advance and obtain your consent through the cookie
            notice before any such services are loaded.
          </p>
        )}

        <h3>8. Contacting us by email</h3>
        <p>
          If you contact us by email, we process your details to handle your enquiry and any follow-up questions. The
          legal basis is our legitimate interest in responding (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR), or Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the
          enquiry relates to a contract. We do not pass this data on without your consent and delete it once it is no
          longer required.
        </p>

        <h3>9. Retention</h3>
        <p>
          Server log files are deleted or anonymised automatically after a short period. Analytics data in Google
          Analytics is deleted after a maximum of 14 months. Your locally stored cookie choice remains until you change
          it or clear site data in your browser.
        </p>

        <h3>10. Your rights</h3>
        <p>You have the right at any time to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>access the personal data we process about you (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
          <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR),</li>
          <li>erasure (Art. 17 GDPR) and restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
          <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR),</li>
          <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR),</li>
          <li>withdraw consent with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR),
          either where you reside or the authority responsible for the controller.
        </p>

        <h3>11. Changes to this privacy policy</h3>
        <p>
          We update this policy whenever our processing or the legal position changes. The version published here, with
          the date shown above, is the one that applies.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
